# Evaluation of collaboration during task completion

When completing complex tasks, it is a good idea to reflect on how we handled the group work and how the group functioned as a whole. We suggest that each group member assess the group work and their own contribution individually, and then share their evaluations and impressions in a five-minute discussion.

## Group functioning (1–5)

*(1 – strongly disagree | 5 – strongly agree)*

✔️ All group members actively participated in the task  
✔️ We listened to one another and respected everyone’s ideas  
✔️ We shared responsibilities equally  
✔️ We made decisions together as a team  
✔️ We supported one another when someone needed help  

## My participation – questions for students (1–5)

*(1 – strongly disagree | 5 – strongly agree)*

✔️ I shared my ideas and opinions  
✔️ I participated in creating the pivot tables  
✔️ I participated in creating the charts  
✔️ I participated in preparing the conclusions  
✔️ I participated in my group’s presentation  

## Teacher assessment of group work

We recommend that the evaluations exchanged in the group are also shared with the teacher at the end. Only then will everyone have a realistic picture of the group’s work and each individual’s contribution.

Checklist for teachers on collaboration during task completion

✔️ all students have a role  
✔️ there is agreement within the group  
✔️ students justify their decisions  
✔️ they help one another  
✔️ they use the digital tool evenly
